worked in a forced labor camp in World War&nbsp;II;

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.560
he was actually forced to work in a brick&nbsp;
making factory. His job is you had the kilns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.780
right, that's making the bricks; and then he&nbsp;
would have to load the bricks onto a trolley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.020
and then he would run that trolley on tracks and&nbsp;
take it to the storage units. So you could just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:34.140
run these bricks to and from the storage units.&nbsp;
The only problem was when these tracks crossed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.640
because when they crossed the trolleys had a&nbsp;
habit of jumping the tracks and spinning the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:44.940
bricks right - oh no, right, what a disaster. So&nbsp;
it did make him think how can we make these tracks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:51.720
